        "original_id": "2c4792ec-0b02-5e5d-be14-3e39e32a3f88",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Oliver Bierhoff, Thomas Helveg, Alberto Zaccheroni\n- Organizations: Udinese Calcio, AC Milan, Germany national football team\n- Events: 1998–99 Udinese Calcio season, UEFA Euro 1996 Final\n- Roles: Topscorer, midfielder, coach, footballer\n\nFacts:\n- Oliver Bierhoff was born on 1 May 1968 and is a retired German footballer.\n- Oliver Bierhoff scored the first golden goal in major international football for Germany in the UEFA Euro 1996 Final.\n- Oliver Bierhoff's performance in the UEFA Euro 1996 Final brought him international prominence.\n- Before the start of the 1998–99 Udinese Calcio season, Udinese Calcio faced setbacks because topscorer Oliver Bierhoff, midfielder Thomas Helveg, and coach Alberto Zaccheroni all left for AC Milan.",
